WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.059 line:91%
Chapter 13. Parent reports, and reading help for students who need it.

00:00:06.478 --> 00:00:09.438 line:91%
Open Results, then the "Parents" tab.

00:00:14.272 --> 00:00:19.840 line:91%
Choose the dates: this month, last month, a semester, the whole year, or your own dates.

00:00:20.295 --> 00:00:28.519 line:91%
There is one report for each student: attendance, behaviour, Test 1 and Test 2, marks, and strong and weak skills.

00:00:28.973 --> 00:00:32.799 line:91%
The app writes a comment for you. Change it as you like.

00:00:33.255 --> 00:00:37.506 line:91%
Below, tips for the parents, in Arabic: how to help at home.

00:00:37.957 --> 00:00:43.944 line:91%
Write the parent's phone number. Then press "WhatsApp". The message is ready: you only press Send.

00:00:44.405 --> 00:00:52.623 line:91%
No WhatsApp? Press "Print". Or "Print all", to print every report on small A5 pages, in Arabic and English.

00:00:53.087 --> 00:00:58.744 line:91%
Now, reading help. Open "Students", and go down to "Reading help and parents".

00:00:59.201 --> 00:01:09.924 line:91%
For a student with dyslexia, or poor eyesight, turn on easy-read letters, big text, or read aloud. Here, Lina gets easy-read letters and big text.

00:01:10.389 --> 00:01:13.844 line:91%
It follows the student on the phone, at once.

00:01:14.295 --> 00:01:19.105 line:91%
Plus 50% gives the student more time in timed questions.

00:01:20.268 --> 00:01:25.665 line:91%
Students can also turn on help themselves. They tap the menu button, then "Aa".

00:01:26.124 --> 00:01:33.025 line:91%
Here the student chooses the text size, easy-read letters, and "Read questions to me". That's it!
